 <comment popup="">Name: AlPackino
Designed by: Ronald Kint-Bruynseels
This puzzle shows how to properly make packing puzzles.
You always should include the box as a piece so that the
program can also check, if the pieces can be moved into the
box. You can also see how to handle multiple identical
pieces. When looking at the solution it is useful to display the
box as a wire frame. This can be done by clicking at the blue
rectangle at the lower end of the tools. The rectangle with
the text &quot;S1 - Box&quot; in it.</comment>
